---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import '../styles/tools.css';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Tools in use"
  description="Software we build to support research and teaching, find expertise, and coordinate the work of a research group."
  active="tools"
  bodyClass="research-page tools-page"
>
  <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Back to home">
    <a href="/"><Arrow /> Home</a>
  </nav>

  <h1>Tools in use</h1>
  <p class="lede">Tools we build to support research, teaching, and the work around them.</p>

  <nav class="research-contents" aria-label="Tools on this page">
    <a href="#placet">Placet</a>
    <a href="#innocompass">InnoCompass</a>
    <a href="#kit-lens">KIT LENS</a>
    <a href="#hub">DSI-WI4 Hub</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="tool-section" id="placet" aria-labelledby="placet-heading">
    <h2 id="placet-heading">Placet</h2>
    <p class="tool-purpose">Keeping the researcher’s decisions visible.</p>
    <div class="tool-copy">
      <p>
        Placet is a desktop app for paper projects in which agents propose and only
        the researcher accepts. Each acceptance is logged in the researcher’s own
        words, so coauthors can follow what changed and why.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m developing Placet and the research-harness plugin it runs on. The desktop
        app is in testing; the plugin’s code and walkthrough are available on GitHub.
      </p>
      <p>
        In my research, agents help develop proposals and prepare literature notes.
        I review the evidence before accepting a change and record why I accepted it.
        For direct quotations, a check compares the wording with the cited page;
        deciding whether the source supports the argument remains my job.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link tool-link" href="https://github.com/DanielHeinz7/research-harness">
      Explore research-harness <Arrow />
    </a>

    <figure class="tool-figure">
      <a href="/images/tools/research-harness-session.png" aria-label="Open the research-harness session view image at full size">
        <img
          src="/images/tools/research-harness-session.png"
          alt="A research-harness session view showing a research question and an open question for the authors to discuss."
          width="1440"
          height="900"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        The research-harness session view, using its public-data example.{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/DanielHeinz7/research-harness/blob/main/docs/media/README.md#where-the-content-comes-from">Demo sources and credits</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="tool-section" id="innocompass" aria-labelledby="innocompass-heading">
    <h2 id="innocompass-heading">InnoCompass</h2>
    <p class="tool-purpose">Making a venture’s assumptions available for discussion.</p>
    <div class="tool-copy">
      <p>
        InnoCompass is an AI-based system for early-stage founders that structures
        how a venture is represented and surfaces the assumptions behind it.
        It is used in KIT’s coaching formats and doubles as our research instrument.
      </p>
      <p>
        I lead the project and its research; technical development is led by my
        doctoral researcher. Our published work asks what AI coaching needs to
        support founders’ learning and judgment.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link tool-link" href="/research/ai-coaching/">
      Read the research behind it <Arrow />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="tool-section" id="kit-lens" aria-labelledby="kit-lens-heading">
    <h2 id="kit-lens-heading">KIT LENS</h2>
    <p class="tool-purpose">Finding the research expertise behind a practical question.</p>
    <div class="tool-copy">
      <p>
        KIT LENS is an AI-assisted prototype that helps people find relevant
        researchers and institutes at KIT. It draws on publications and other
        research material to suggest who might be able to help with an inquiry.
      </p>
      <p>
        Developed through a master’s thesis in our lab, it was tested in a limited
        pilot with KIT staff. The aim is to give them a starting point for
        identifying expertise and deciding whom to contact.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tool-section" id="hub" aria-labelledby="hub-heading">
    <h2 id="hub-heading">DSI-WI4 Hub</h2>
    <p class="tool-purpose">Bringing the work of a research group together.</p>
    <div class="tool-copy">
      <p>
        A research group runs research, teaching, projects, and administration across
        many tools. I’m building the DSI-WI4 Hub at KIT to connect that work through
        a shared sign-in and apps for meetings, publications, and internal processes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The group uses the hub in its everyday work. Access to its apps is managed
        through the group’s accounts and permissions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <a href="/lab/">Inside the lab <Arrow /></a>
    <a href="/teaching/">Teaching <Arrow /></a>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
